      "document": "Monitoring training load - session RPE and the limits of load ratios",
      "section": "Session RPE training load",
      "text": "Session RPE quantifies training load by multiplying the person's rating of perceived exertion for the whole session, on a 0 to 10 scale, by the session duration in minutes. The product can be summed across a week to track load (Foster 2001).",
      "publisher": "Peer-reviewed sports science literature",
      "citation": "Foster C et al. A new approach to monitoring exercise training. J Strength Cond Res 2001;15(1):109-115. Impellizzeri FM et al. Acute:Chronic Workload Ratio: Conceptual Issues and Fundamental Pitfalls. Int J Sports Physiol Perform 2020;15(6):907-913.",
